					<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
						The Richardson annular effect causes early flow deceleration and boundary layer reversal near the vessel wall while the core still moves forward. This creates low and oscillatory wall shear stress (OSI &gt; 0.3), the proven mechanical trigger for focal atheromatous plaque formation in the carotid bifurcation.
